    "analysis": "The active task is Problem D, implemented in src/permutations.cc. Shared contract: read through EOF, remove exactly the six whitespace characters recognized by the source, preserve native char ordering, and emit every distinct permutation in lexicographic order as \"[ \" followed by each character and a space, then \"]\\n\". Empty filtered input emits nothing. For nonempty length n and P distinct permutations, output requires P(2n+4) bytes, so exhaustive output cannot be bypassed. The baseline passed four cases and averaged 0.132437 seconds, with samples spanning 0.131519–0.133778 seconds. There is no profile or workload-size evidence. Per-character stream insertion and per-row flushing are therefore strong optimization hypotheses, not measured bottlenecks. Prioritize buffering, then generation/formatting fusion; investigate parallelism cautiously on the four-core ARM64 CPU because output serialization and short runtimes may erase its benefits."
